## About

Nova is a chat companion that remembers things about you, looks at your pictures, talks and listens, and can change her personality. Everything she saves stays in small local files on your own computer, with no database or cloud storage to set up.

## Features

| | Feature | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| 🌸 | **Kawaii UI** | Clean pastel interface with kaomojis in the headers and chat |
| 🧠 | **Long-term memory** | Save facts about yourself to a local JSON file so Nova remembers you between sessions |
| 📝 | **Quick notes sidebar** | Keep snippets, ideas and to-do lists inside the app |
| 👀 | **Multimodal vision** | Upload photos (outfits, ingredients, plants, code screenshots) and Nova analyzes them |
| 🎙️ | **Voice loop** | Talk with your microphone (`streamlit-mic-recorder`) and hear replies through `gTTS` |
| 🌍 | **Multi-language** | English, Spanish, French, Japanese, Hindi and German for text, speech recognition and audio |
| 🎭 | **Custom personalities** | Friendly and Casual, Witty and Sarcastic Friend, Wise Zen Mentor, Hyper-Supportive Cheerleader, Strict Coding Coach |

## Tech stack

- **Frontend:** [Streamlit](https://streamlit.io/)
- **AI engine:** Google GenAI SDK (`google-genai`) with a Gemini model
- **Voice:** `gTTS` for text-to-speech and `streamlit-mic-recorder` for speech-to-text
- **Storage:** local JSON files (`memory.json`, `notes.json`)

## Getting started

### 1. Clone the project

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Meo-ow0/Nova-your-personal-AI-companion-.git
cd Nova-your-personal-AI-companion-
```

### 2. Install the dependencies

```bash
pip install streamlit google-genai gtts pillow streamlit-mic-recorder
```

### 3. Add your API key

Nova needs a Gemini API key from [Google AI Studio](https://aistudio.google.com/). Keep it private and never commit it to GitHub. Set it as an environment variable or in a local secrets file, the same way `app.py` expects it.

### 4. Run the app

```bash
streamlit run app.py
```

Then open the local link that Streamlit prints in your terminal.

## Project files

| File | What it does |
|---|---|
| `app.py` | The main Streamlit app |
| `memory.json` | Facts Nova remembers about you (created when you use the app) |
| `notes.json` | Your quick notes (created when you use the app) |

## Privacy

- Memory and notes are stored only in local files on your computer.
- Add `memory.json`, `notes.json` and any secrets file to `.gitignore` so your personal data and API key never get uploaded.
- Chat text, photos and voice are sent to Google's API to get a reply, so don't share anything you want to keep private.

